Z||000000||Nashco||12-03-2001||01:45 AM||||I just got this month's newsletter from Held Motorsports, and they are having a group discount sale on rear coilovers.  The group buy increases in amount for every person who goes in on it...here's how it works:  for every one person who is included in the group buy, $1 is subtracted from each unit price.  If 30 people go in on the deal, that's thirty dollars off for EACH person!<P>I've emailed Dave to clarify a few things, but I wanted to get a quick note out to everybody who is interested.  I, coincidentally, was planning on buying a set of coilovers this month, probably around Christmas..a gift to myself <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>So how many people are interested in going in on the group buy?  Remember, the more people who go in, the better the prices are.  You may not want new coilovers this month, but in six months you may be buying them for 30 or 40 bucks more!  It's just a perk of the group buy <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I have a quick numbering system I've thought up, so we can see how many people will likely go in on it.  Please give a "quick reference" number in your post to let me/us know where you stand:<P>1 - Definitely will be buying<BR>2 - Probably will buy, despite cost outcome<BR>3 - Maybe will buy if enough other people do to bring prices down<BR>4 - Probably won't, unless enough people do it to bring prices way down<BR>5 - I like the pretty paint on new parts, but I'm too cheap to actually purchase them<P>I myself am a 1, definitely will be buying.  I may have to break the bank doing it (too many expenses lately), but I can't drive my car as it is anymore.<P>Oh, in case you were wondering, some general prices are as follows:<P>KYB Rear Coilovers (84-88)___________$465<BR>Bilstein Rear Coilovers (84-88)______$768<BR>Koni Rear Coilovers (84-88)__________$870<P>For 84-87 cars with 88 rear suspensions, add 60 dollars.<P>I will be buying the KYBs, as that will work for now.  Later down the road I plan on the Konis, but after I've done more with my car (different motor installed, chassis lightening, body work, etc.)<P>I'm hoping there is a fair amount of people who will entertain this, we shall see <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||4
