Z||000009||Nashco||12-03-2001||05:12 PM||||Tigger, these are for all years.  The prices above are for all years (they are the same price if for 84-87 or 88), just cost a smidge EXTRA if you have 88 in 84-87 chassis.<P>rodmcneill: A fair idea, but if we get, say, 60 people to go in on it, we're way better than 10%.<P>Ha, I didn't think about getting an outrageous amount of people involved..lol.  I highly doubt that many would even commit, but it's a thought.  Even if we could only get 100 people to seriously commit, that's still A HUNDRED BUCKS!  I am curious as to how Dave Held would respond if we had 300 people in our group buy....a sticky situation for him, as it would be hard to even break even, if at all possible.  I suppose he would gain a lot of business afterwards, but I'll have to ask him if there's a maximum as well.<P>Ok, here's the count so far:<P>1s - 1<BR>2s - 1<BR>3s - 2<BR>4s - 1<BR>5s - Ha, I won't count you guys  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>Keep the numbers coming!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>*edited typo*<p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 12-03-2001).]||||reg||1
