Z||000023||85ZainoGT||12-04-2001||09:27 PM||||ok, so this is only going to lower my rear end then?  what about the front?<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 GT all the options :)<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpicNEW2b.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000024||Nashco||12-05-2001||12:27 AM||||Daleford - I didn't think to ask about that, but his email pointed right to the conversion kit page.  I have emailed and asked, should have an answer soon.<P>85ZainoGT - Well, this will only lower your rear end if you adjust it to do so.  You can get a 12" spring and adjust from stock rear height to 2" lowered, as cadero2dmax explained.  So, you could have it at stock height or only 1" lowered in the rear until you lower the front, then adjust them accordingly.  That's why they're so great; if you're going for ride height they're progressive.  In the future if you want to lower it even more(say, from 2" lowered to 4" lowered), you only have to buy another set of springs and swap them out!<P>I have already lowered my front about 1.5", so I will probably get 10" springs so I can adjust from 2" to 4" lowering.<P>I know there are more out there wanting this deal!  Remember, this will be very cheap if all those people who want them for cheap get them!  There isn't any commitment here, but if you're interested, even only a #4, please say so!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
