Z||000041||Nashco||12-09-2001||12:06 AM||||Daleford, as far as the minimum strut height, the best way to know that is to measure the length of the strut at full compression.  I'd imagine the suspension has enough travel to bottom out the strut with the springs adjusted properly.<P>I am not familiar enough with the drivetrain yet to know how you can change strut location.  After I do the job, I'll probably know <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Oh yeah...and if you *want* to be a 1, don't let others affect it so much...do it!!!  You know you'll be glad you did after you do it <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I sent an email out to a few Fiero email lists just a bit ago, hopefully that generates some more interest...<P>Thanks guys, and keep me updated!  In a few days here I'll be submitting my order to Dave at Held Motorsports.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
