Z||000048||Nashco||12-09-2001||02:47 PM||||GKDINC:  Got you down as a 1.  Like Daleford said, Dave will gladly help you with a recommended spring for your exact application.  Your spring rate and size depends on your motor, application, and what ride height and quality is desired.<P>1s - 5<BR>2s - 2<BR>3s - 9<BR>4s - 2<P>puter2K:  Dave said that as the orders come in he will keep track of the running total discount.  Near the end of the month he'll let everybody know how many orders have been made and what discount to expect.  When you make your order, explain that you are part of the group purchase, and you'd like him to let you know at the end of the month what the final price is.<P>Boomtastic:  Ha, well hopefully you end up getting some...you won't regret it after you do!  Think "full adjustability"....<P>I'm assuming that he's building the kits as they come in if there's more orders than expected, but we can expect the parts before too long, end of January max.  My car will be parked for a few months, so time isn't too big of a deal.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>*added off-list 3*<p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 12-09-2001).]||||reg||1
